R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3];K=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;B=K/'batches/edition-23';S=R/'projects/site';now=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()
q=json.loads((K/'queue.json').read_text());assert q['active_batch'] is None;assert not (B/'batch.json').exists();B.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
rows=[(454, 'yesterday-left-on-the-chair', 'Yesterday left on the chair', 'The poem steps into the present carrying echoes of the past. A worn outdoor coat left on a chair near morning light suggests a transition already beginning, without literal star maps, swallows or a heroic figure.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 quiet matte oil-pastel and gouache interior. The cropped back of one simple wooden chair at left carries a plain soft grey-blue outdoor coat, its shoulders folded over the chair back and hem hanging naturally, no person inside it. Some morning light from an off-frame doorway reaches the nearest fold and a patch of ordinary floor; the rest of the right half is empty pale room space. The chair seat is only partly visible, legs may be cropped; believable wooden construction and fabric compression where it meets the back. No hat, suitcase, books, clock, star map, birds, person, window panorama, text or picturesque decay. Coat has modest ordinary wear but no decorative tears. Suggest someone beginning their day and leaving yesterday’s weight behind; emotionally open, not a staged fashion display.'), (457, 'paper-kept-for-a-poem', 'Paper kept for a poem', 'The speaker has kept a blank sheet in a pocket, waiting for poetry to return before the paper tears. A close drawing of the folded sheet and pocket preserves that fragile patience without showing an invented poet.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 spare graphite drawing with a little muted warm-grey watercolor: close crop of an ordinary pale cotton shirt folded flat on a surface, only its breast-pocket area visible at left and centre. A small folded blank paper peeks above the pocket opening, its top edge slightly softened from time, one tiny dog-ear and a clear crease; absolutely no writing, ruled lines or printed marks. Pocket seams connect consistently to shirt fabric, two soft gravity-led folds elsewhere, no buttons or body needed in the crop. Right half quiet pale paper-like background, selectively resolved pencil lines only around the pocket mouth and paper fold. No pen, book, ink bottle, floral props, human silhouette or portrait. The paper remains usable and intact, not shredded; tenderness of a waiting poem.'), (461, 'faith-in-the-pathless-wood', 'Faith in the pathless wood', 'The speaker is lost in deep woods yet keeps praying for light. An obstructed view through ordinary trees preserves uncertainty and faith without inventing Krishna, a luminous apparition or a completed rescue.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 restrained cool green and blue-grey gouache forest study at late dusk. View from within an ordinary dense wood: a few unequal tree trunks at varied distances, low branches partially crossing the view, leaf masses overlap into dark but readable shapes. A narrow gap between trunks at centre right offers a small patch of slightly lighter natural evening sky far away, not a glowing doorway or path. Near ground has a few roots and leaf litter only where visible; no clear trail, no perfect leading line, no theatrical fog or sun beams. Geometry of trunks and branches continuous, depth comes from simple overlapping matte planes and progressively quieter detail. No deity, person, face, animal, shrine, grand wall, stars, candles or text. A searching uncertainty with room for faith; do not resolve it into magical rescue or horror imagery.')]
items=[]
for pid,ident,title,reason,scene in rows:
 p=S/f'content/editions/issue-23/poem-{pid}.json';d=json.loads(p.read_text());snapshot=B/f'poem-{pid}.json';snapshot.write_bytes(p.read_bytes())
 prompt=f'Use case: illustration-story. Original horizontal 3:2 literary artwork for Kabita Live Issue23. Human Natural in Poetic Natural mode. Preserve the selected expressive medium; a painted interpretation, never documentary evidence.\nEmotional anchor: {reason}\nScene and medium: {scene}\nAnti-optimization checks: avoid staged object display, equal detail everywhere, mechanically repeated shapes, theatrical lighting and cosmetic distress. Material contact, geometry and illumination must make sense. Preserve quiet negative space and emotional ambiguity. No identifiable real people, portraits, readable text, signature, logos or watermark. No people, portraits or documentary location claims. Opaque ivory-paper background.\nPoem {d["title"]} by {d["author"]}; source read fully, use as context only, never render the words:\n{d["text"]}\n'
